<http://data.silknow.org/object/b1ddb54b-0807-38c6-b686-3c70437f98bc/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Cruciform textile panel of embroidered linen canvas with silk and silver-gilt threads. A representation of a black and white dog, shown sideways (facing to the left) occupies the most of the panel. It is topped by a red scroll bearing the inscription \"Jupiter\" (all in capital letters). The entire ground has a geometrical  pattern consisting of the series of rhomboid fields embroidered in blue, green, white, ochre and beige silks. In the section between the dog and the scroll, a monogram (MR) is embroidered in silks matching the ones in the ground, which makes it hard to notice at a first galnce. The panel is edged with a raised border of silver-gilt embroidery."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/b1ddb54b-0807-38c6-b686-3c70437f98bc> .

